title: "agents-work — how every agent works in this garden: the gardener's standing instructions"
summary: "The agents' work agreement: the gardener's standing instructions to every agent that works in this garden, one clause each. A clause that names a guard (core/law/guards.yaml) is checked at the agent's own door before each act, and the act it forbids is refused there (bin/hook.py). The gardener changes a clause by their own word."
statements:
  - say:        { by: @@GARDENER@@, at: now }
  - own:        { by: @@GARDENER@@, of: self }
  - can:        { id: quoted-text, by: { someone: session }, of: "give an interpreter its text inside another interpreter's quotes" }
  - forbidden:  { id: one-text-one-parser, of: quoted-text, through: self, clause: { guard: one-text-one-parser } }
  - can:        { id: commands-in-bash, by: { someone: session }, of: "run its commands in bash, 5.0 or later" }
  - obligatory: { id: shell-is, of: commands-in-bash, through: self, clause: { guard: shell-is, operand: { shell: bash, floor: "5.0" } } }
  - can:        { id: memory-writes, by: { someone: session }, of: "write into a harness's memory folder what belongs in the garden" }
  - forbidden:  { id: no-memory-write, of: memory-writes, through: self, clause: { guard: no-memory-write } }
---
What every agent working in this garden is bound by, as its gardener says it. These three clauses are the seed's: a new
garden starts with them.

- **One text, one parser.** A command is read by one shell, the garden's. Text meant for another interpreter, such as
  another shell, PowerShell, Python, a remote host or a journal entry's body, goes to it as a file, on standard input,
  or as one argument. It is never carried inside another interpreter's quotes.
- **The shell is bash, 5.0 or later.** The agent's harness runs its commands in bash. `python3 bin/hook.py install
  claude-code` sets it in this clone's own settings.
- **Nothing in a harness's memory.** What an agent learns goes into the garden, where every agent after it reads it: a
  fact as a statement on the bean it is about, a standing instruction as a clause here that the gardener says. Where
  the work stands is read, never stored: `python3 bin/now.py`. A write into the harness's memory folder is refused.

To lift a clause, say its contradictory: `permitted` of `quoted-text` or of `memory-writes`, or `omissible` of
`commands-in-bash`, each a clause naming the same guard. To change one, change its operand, for example another shell or
another floor. The law's other guards (core/law/guards.yaml) hold where the gardener names them in a clause here, with
the operand each takes: the hosts, the columns, the files.
